{"schema_version":1,"stream":"steps","idempotency_key":"step:run_bf10663c0a8a:git:commit:1:2","created_at":"2026-09-23 19:04:33","provenance":"recorded","origin":{"recorder":{"installation_id":"eca1b52d-1c4f-4337-9c73-d8c035d3b08c"},"performer":{"kind":"system","role":"cli"}},"payload":{"step_name":"git:commit","phase":"1","iteration":2,"result_json":{"hash":"066cd996f540b688e08c9339213e9f9244093752","short_hash":"066cd99","message":"review: plan 210 phase 1 execution binding","files":["5x-cli/docs/development/reviews/run_bf10663c0a8a-phase-1-review.md","docs/development/runs/210-implementation-review-governance-plan/run_bf10663c0a8a/steps.jsonl"]},"head_commit":"066cd996f540b688e08c9339213e9f9244093752","patch_id":"8ee48f5a6ac6341b1c57af53c4c0e4d8349c36dc","diff_summary":{"files_changed":2,"insertions":100,"deletions":0},"duration_ms":null,"tokens_in":null,"tokens_out":null,"cost_usd":null,"model":null}}
{"schema_version":1,"stream":"steps","idempotency_key":"step:run_bf10663c0a8a:reviewer:commit:1:0","created_at":"2026-09-23 19:04:52","provenance":"recorded","origin":{"recorder":{"installation_id":"eca1b52d-1c4f-4337-9c73-d8c035d3b08c"},"performer":{"kind":"agent","role":"reviewer","provider":"claude-code"}},"payload":{"step_name":"reviewer:commit","phase":"1","iteration":0,"result_json":{"readiness":"not_ready","summary":"The binding model is solid and consistent with plan 209, and all 3624 tests, typecheck and lint pass. But canonical-vs-worktree path handling breaks binding for every worktree-mapped run (P0), and the drift policy rejects the workflow's own post-approval plan edits, so this plan cannot bind its own execution run (P1, needs a human decision).","items":[{"id":"R1","title":"Worktree-mapped execution runs cannot bind: plan identity and approved-byte read use the wrong path","action":"auto_fix","reason":"render/invoke/bind pass the worktree effectivePlanPath as canonical identity, and planPathsIdentifySamePlan(canonical, worktree) is false, so there are zero candidates and explicit bind is refused. The record path reads bytes from the control-plane checkout, and showPlanAtCommit falls back to git show <c>:/abs/path, which returns null (IMPLEMENTATION_APPROVED_PLAN_UNAVAILABLE). Both verified against run_bf10663c0a8a. Fix: use run.plan_path for identity, effectivePlanPath for current bytes, and a controlPlaneRoot-relative repo path for approved bytes (relativePathUnder); add a worktree-mapped integration test.","priority":"P0"},{"id":"R2","title":"Drift policy rejects workflow-owned post-approval plan edits (status header, Phase 0 note); this plan cannot bind its own run","action":"human_required","reason":"The approved commit is the reviewer head (2c23519). The later mark-reviewed Status edit (22a8dee) and the Phase 0 verification paragraph the plan requires (abaa379) are non-checkbox drift; detectPlanDrift returns drifted:true for this repo, so binding fails even in advisory mode. Choose a policy: anchor to the source run final commit, normalize workflow-owned spans, move notes to run records, or add an interim human amendment path.","priority":"P1"},{"id":"R3","title":"normalizeCheckboxState rewrites every [x]/[ ] in the document, not only task-list markers","action":"auto_fix","reason":"Edits such as arr[x] vs arr[ ] in code or prose are hidden from drift detection. Anchor the regex to list-item checkbox markers and add a unit case.","priority":"P2"},{"id":"R4","title":"No tests for template render / invoke implementation admission gating","action":"auto_fix","reason":"The template.handler and invoke.handler gating, including the RecordContextError IMPLEMENTATION_APPROVAL_REQUIRED fallback and -continued template selection, is untested; only the record path and bind are covered. Mirror the existing plan-review render/invoke parity tests.","priority":"P2"},{"id":"R5","title":"Integration test claims source removal/rebuild but never rebuilds the index","action":"auto_fix","reason":"The test deletes the source run dir but runs no records rebuild, and records/index-rebuild.ts (listed in Phase 1 Files) is unchanged. Add a rebuild step or correct the checklist wording.","priority":"P2"}]},"head_commit":"066cd996f540b688e08c9339213e9f9244093752","patch_id":null,"diff_summary":{"files_changed":0,"insertions":0,"deletions":0},"duration_ms":560841,"tokens_in":58,"tokens_out":17016,"cost_usd":1.5129008000000002,"model":"claude-opus-5-5"}}
{"schema_version":1,"stream":"steps","idempotency_key":"step:run_bf10663c0a8a:human:gate:1:1","created_at":"2026-09-23 19:07:06","provenance":"recorded","origin":{"recorder":{"installation_id":"eca1b52d-1c4f-4337-9c73-d8c035d3b08c"},"performer":{"kind":"human","role":"operator"}},"payload":{"step_name":"human:gate","phase":"1","iteration":1,"result_json":{"choice":"continue","guidance":"Approval drift policy: anchor approved plan bytes to the source plan-review run’s finalized plan commit (including its workflow Status update), validating recorded terminal approval and final-correction evidence; later edits remain drift. Move Phase 0 verification prose out of the plan into run records, retain checklist completion. Fix the worktree canonical identity/current-byte/approved-byte P0 bug and all mechanical P2 issues identified in the phase-1 review. Add end-to-end tests for the real source-finalization and worktree paths. Do not infer approval from arbitrary later HEAD."},"head_commit":"066cd996f540b688e08c9339213e9f9244093752","patch_id":null,"diff_summary":{"files_changed":0,"insertions":0,"deletions":0},"duration_ms":null,"tokens_in":null,"tokens_out":null,"cost_usd":null,"model":null}}
